  "context_pill": "Section 35ABB Amortisation",
  "example_summary": "Easy Call Ltd. acquires a 10-year telecom licence paid in 3 instalments, computing deduction for A.Y. 2026-27.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Summary Matrix: Section 35ABB\n\n| Statutory Parameter | Legal Rule & Condition | Tax Treatment | Deductibility Benchmark |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Nature of Expenditure** | Any capital expenditure actually paid for acquiring telecommunication licences | Allowed as amortised deduction | Spread equally over active licence period |\n| **Timing: Payment Before Commencement** | Payment made before business commences | Deduction begins in the **year of commencement of business** | Spread over remaining unexpired period |\n| **Timing: Payment After Commencement** | Payment made after business commences | Deduction begins in the **year of actual payment** | Spread over remaining unexpired period |\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Duration of Deduction: The deduction continues until the final year in which the licence ceases to be in force. Unexpired period is computed from the relevant previous year until the date of licence expiry.\n\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Actual Payment Condition: Deduction u/s 35ABB strictly requires **actual payment**. Mere liability or provision accrued does not trigger amortisation until cash outflow occurs.",
